---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ResourceRow from '../components/ResourceRow.astro';
import SignupForm from '../components/SignupForm.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { startHere } from '../data/resources';
const { group, organizer } = site;
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>{site.tagline}</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      We think advanced AI may be one of the most consequential technologies of this century, and
      that whether it goes well is still an open question. We run a reading group each term and
      help students find their way into the field. No prerequisites, and everyone at Dartmouth is
      welcome.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/#sign-up">Sign up for the reading group&nbsp;→</a>
      <a class="button" href={site.groupMeUrl}>Join the GroupMe</a>
      <a href={site.bookingUrl}>Book a time with {organizer.short}</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="reading-group">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>The {site.term} reading group</h2>
      <span>Six Monday evenings, dinner included</span>
    </div>
    <div class="list">
      <div class="row kv"><span class="k sc">when</span><span class="v">{group.when}. Exact time set by who signs up</span></div>
      <div class="row kv"><span class="k sc">length</span><span class="v">{group.length}</span></div>
      <div class="row kv"><span class="k sc">format</span><span class="v">{group.format}</span></div>
      <div class="row kv"><span class="k sc">who</span><span class="v">{group.who}</span></div>
      <div class="row kv"><span class="k sc">size</span><span class="v">{group.size}</span></div>
      <div class="row kv"><span class="k sc">cost</span><span class="v">{group.cost}</span></div>
    </div>
    <h3 class="sub">What we'll cover</h3>
    <ol class="weeks">
      {group.curriculum.map((w) => (
        <li>
          <span class="wk sc">week {w.week}</span>
          <span class="t">{w.title}{w.note && <span class="n"> · {w.note}</span>}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p class="note">
      The plan is to leave with a real understanding of why people worry about this, what the
      strongest counterarguments are, and where you'd go next if you wanted to work on it. Readings
      are still being chosen and the outline may shift. If more people want in than fit, I'll run a
      second group.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/#sign-up">Sign up&nbsp;→</a>
      <a href={site.bookingUrl}>Not sure? Book a time to talk it over</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SignupForm />

  <section class="section" id="start-here">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Start here</h2>
      <span>Three things to read before anything else</span>
    </div>
    <div class="list">
      {startHere.map((item) => <ResourceRow item={item} />)}
    </div>
    <a href="/resources/" style="font-size: 16.5px;">All resources&nbsp;→</a>
  </section>
</Base>
